Nodejs {{{1

Fedora package:  nodejs-np
Default package location: /usr/lib/node_modules/

REVIEW ACCURACY OF BELOW

Use nvm to install node
	https://nodejs.org/en/download
	Download for nvm install on Linux
	curl -o- https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nvm-sh/nvm/v0.40.5/install.sh | bash

Install node
	nvm install latest
	Is installed to ~/.local/share/nvm/v26.3.1/bin/node
	Symlink to .local/bin

Local location when using NVM (Node Version Manager):  ~/.nvm/versions/node/<version>/lib/node_modules
Local executables: ~/.nvm/versions/node/<version>/bin/

apps including npm installed in  ~/.local/share/nvm/v26.4.0/lib/node_modules/
app shortcuts in ~/.local/share/nvm/v26.4.0/bin

Show root location: npm root -g
Show executable location: npm bin -g
Locate npm install location: npm config get prefix
list installed packages: npm list -g

Fish shell compatible version of NVM:  
	fisher install jorgebucaran/nvm.fish
	adds path to nvm script at ~/.config/nvm


